course: dictionary
lesson: 13108
title: Flatlined: from hospital to business
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words travel. «Flatlined» began in hospitals, where a heart monitor shows a wavy line for each heartbeat. When the heart stops, the line goes flat, so doctors say it flatlined. Today people use it in other ways too, so you need the context to know which meaning fits.
explain: «Sales of the toy have flatlined since March.» Sales cannot have a heartbeat, so flatlined here does not mean died. The clues are sales and since March. Flatlined means the sales stopped growing and stayed at the same level.
explain: People also use flatlined for themselves when they are very tired. «After the long school trip, we were all flatlined.» Nobody had stopped breathing. The children had no energy left, just like a line that is flat and still. Always check: does my meaning fit the whole sentence?
fact: Flatlined is a verb: flatline, flatlines, flatlined, flatlining.
fact: A flatline is also a noun: «The screen showed a flatline.»
fact: «Flatlined» means stopped growing or stayed at the same level, as in «sales have flatlined».
fact: «Flatlined» can also mean very tired, with no energy left. This is informal, so save it for chatting, not for your essays.
fact: In hospitals, «flatlined» means the heart has stopped. It is slang and can sound blunt, so be gentle when you talk about it with others.
exercise: «Sales of the toy have flatlined since March.» What does flatlined mean here? | Was thrown in the bin | *Stopped growing, staying at the same level | Went up very fast | Was sold for a lot of money
exercise: In a hospital drama, the heart monitor flatlined. What does this mean? | The doctor was smiling | The heart was beating very fast | The patient was asleep | *The heart had stopped
exercise: «After the long school trip, we were all flatlined.» What does flatlined suggest? | Hungry for lunch | *Very tired, with no energy left | Angry at the bus driver | Full of energy and ready to run
test: «The town's population has flatlined for ten years.» What does flatlined mean? | Moved to the sea | Grew very fast | *Stayed at the same level
test: The graph showed a flatline. What is a flatline? | A bendy road | A bowl of soup | A tall tree | *A flat, unchanging line
exam: Which sentence means the same as «the sales stopped growing»? | *Sales have flatlined | Sales have run away | Sales have been wrapped up | Sales have skyrocketed
